<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Cenomani</h1><p class="st-meta">400 BCE – 89 BCE (approx.) · capital Brixia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Celtic people of the plain around Brescia and Verona who, unlike other Cisalpine Gauls, were usually allies of Rome.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a> describes the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aulerci-cenomani">Cenomani</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gauls</a> who crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> under a leader named Elitovius in the 5th or 4th century BCE and settled in the lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brescia">Brixia</a> (<a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-brescia">Brescia</a>) and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-verona">Verona</a>, between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/insubres">Insubres</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/veneti">Veneti</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brescia">Brixia</a> was their main centre. They farmed the plain and traded with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/veneti">Veneti</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruscans">Etruscans</a>. Their relations with their Celtic neighbours were often hostile, and in 225 BCE they joined the Veneti in sending troops to help <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/insubres">Insubres</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/boii">Boii</a>. Apart from joining a revolt in 200–197 BCE, they remained Roman allies.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After 197 BCE the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aulerci-cenomani">Cenomani</a> stayed loyal and were gradually Romanised. Their towns received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> rights in 89 BCE and full citizenship in 49 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brescia">Brixia</a> became a Roman colony and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-verona">Verona</a> a leading town of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 400 BCE – 89 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:51.74%;width:6.19%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>400 BCE – 89 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Brixia</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cisalpine Cenomani</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-244&amp;focus=cenomani" aria-label="Cenomani on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4923 572 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Cenomani lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5243 828L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5243 828h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5243 828h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Brixia. <a href="/atlas?year=-244&amp;focus=cenomani">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

